---
import { Card } from "@bundu/ui/ui/card";
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";

/**
 * The map. One row per public repository in `mzizi-dev`, with what it holds and
 * what it serves. Private repositories are not listed, including the one that
 * operates the MCP server — the endpoint is public and is named, the source is
 * not.
 *
 * `state` is deliberately not a marketing word. "shipping code" means the
 * repository holds a working implementation; "serving" additionally means a
 * hostname resolves to it; "placeholder" means a README and nothing else.
 * `site`, when set, is the live hostname a repository serves.
 * These were checked with `dig` and the GitHub API, not assumed.
 */
const repos = [
  {
    name: "mzizi",
    role: "The language",
    state: "shipping code, not routed",
    body: "The Mzizi programming language, and Phase 0 of its research charter (v0.4, “Mzizi: a general-purpose programming language”): the language's design (the charter and the RFCs, RFC-0001 to RFC-0012, with 0005 reserved), LANGUAGE-TRACKER.md (what the language still has to build, against Python, Go, C++, TypeScript and Rust), and the toolchain that implements it: the mz compiler front end — lexer, recovering parser, resolver, agent diagnostic protocol and mz fix, content-addressed IR, and mz build, which lowers a service (and only a service) to a local Rust + axum package — nine primitives and an example service written in Mzizi itself, and the public half of the benchmark harness, including the kill-criterion driver. The kill-criterion run has not happened. Rust.",
    href: "/language",
    internal: true,
  },
  {
    name: "mzizi-registry",
    role: "The components: design system and registry",
    state: "shipping code; its files are what api.mzizi.dev serves",
    body: "The components built to support the language, as its UI layer: the canonical component registry for the Mzizi ecosystem, shadcn-compatible and installable with the shadcn CLI. Also the brand system, the design tokens, the DNA double helix the frontend architecture is organised around, and Mzizi Roots, the Rust components: ten crates on crates.io at 0.1.0, with mzizi-roots (UI) and mzizi-roots-server (server) as the umbrellas. It also holds the component contracts (contracts/): a versioned, machine-readable contract for each of the Mzizi Dashboard Standard's 31 app components in @bundu/ui. Its files are what api.mzizi.dev serves (through mzizi-api-gateway), and it holds no database. TypeScript and Rust.",
  },
  {
    name: "mzizi-api-gateway",
    role: "The registry API",
    state: "serving api.mzizi.dev today",
    site: "https://api.mzizi.dev/v1",
    body: "Serves api.mzizi.dev: the registry API as a Hono Cloudflare Worker (TypeScript). Every route answers from the registry's repository files, generated at a pinned registry commit and bundled into the Worker. A bot moves that pin to registry main (checked hourly, merged only when CI and strict parity against production pass; mzizi-api-gateway#16), so the commit changes without an edit here: every response's x-mzizi-source header names the one being served. There's no origin, no database and no Supabase. It replaced the registry's own Worker on 2026-09-29 with zero unexplained differences in a 1,359-request parity check.",
  },
  {
    name: "mzizi-console",
    role: "The console",
    state: "serving app.mzizi.dev today",
    site: "https://app.mzizi.dev",
    body: "app.mzizi.dev — Astro renders the chrome as static HTML, Rust/Dioxus islands render the live data from the registry API. Replaces an earlier Svelte mini-app: the doctrine is one UI framework, Astro, with Rust first and TypeScript second underneath.",
  },
  {
    name: "mzizi-site",
    role: "This site",
    state: "serving mzizi.dev today",
    site: "https://mzizi.dev",
    body: "The front door and the agent-facing surfaces — llms.txt and the MCP card. Astro, static output, deployed as a Cloudflare Worker with static assets, serving the mzizi.dev apex.",
  },
  {
    name: "mzizi-docs",
    role: "Documentation",
    state: "serving docs.mzizi.dev today",
    body: "The Mintlify documentation site, live at docs.mzizi.dev (HTTP 200, checked 2026-09-27). It is the one home of Mzizi's documentation — the language, the registry, design foundations, patterns, blocks and charts.",
    site: "https://docs.mzizi.dev",
  },
  {
    name: "mzizi-roadmap",
    role: "Roadmap",
    state: "placeholder",
    body: "The Mzizi roadmap. An empty repository with a one-line README at the time of writing; the real plan of record is CHARTER.md in the language repository.",
  },
];
---

<Site
  title="Ecosystem"
  description="Every public repository in the Mzizi ecosystem: the language, then the components, the API gateway, the console, the docs and this site that support it — with what each one actually holds today."
  lede="Seven public repositories. Four serve a live hostname; the rest are code that is built but not routed, or a placeholder. This page says which is which."
>
  <p>
    Mzizi is a programming language. Its ecosystem is governed by{" "}
    <strong>Mzizi</strong>, which owns the language, its toolchain and its
    components outright and operates the registry and tooling day-to-day. Everything listed here is public and Apache-2.0.
    There are private repositories in the org too — they are not listed, and
    neither is anything that is not yet real.
  </p>

  {
    repos.map((r) => (
      <Card className="flow my-6">
        <h2>
          {r.name} <span class="state">— {r.role}</span>
        </h2>
        <p>{r.body}</p>
        <p class="state">
          State: {r.state} ·{" "}
          <a href={`https://github.com/mzizi-dev/${r.name}`}>source</a>
          {r.site && (
            <>
              {" · "}
              <a href={r.site}>{new URL(r.site).host}</a>
            </>
          )}
          {r.href && (
            <>
              {" · "}
              <a href={r.href}>more on this site</a>
            </>
          )}
        </p>
      </Card>
    ))
  }

  <h2>The one live agent endpoint</h2>

  <p>
    <code>https://mcp.mzizi.dev/mcp</code> is an MCP server over Streamable HTTP,
    serving the component registry as whole documents — one call returns
    everything about a component rather than several, plus the skills and the
    docs. It is Rust first: where a component has a Mzizi Roots implementation,{" "}
    <code>mzizi_get_component</code> leads with it (the crate, the{" "}
    <code>cargo add</code> line, the contract and the <code>.rs</code> source)
    and gives the React build second, and <code>mzizi_list_components</code>{" "}
    takes a <code>rust</code> filter. It is free with no sign-in, except the
    Fundi tools, which file into the console's issue desk and need a console
    user. That is the owner's decision of 2026-09-29, and it is live:{" "}
    <code>mzizi-mcp</code> 0.11.2 answers <code>initialize</code>,{" "}
    <code>tools/list</code> and the component tools with no token, and only{" "}
    <code>mzizi_fundi</code> and <code>mzizi_report_issue</code> ask for
    sign-in (checked 2026-09-30). Its source is not public, so it has no row
    above.
  </p>

  <p>
    Discover its tools with the standard <code>tools/list</code> request. Any
    list of tool names written on a web page — including this one — can go
    stale, and the server is the only thing that knows what it currently
    exposes.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    For anything about Mzizi — the language, the components, this site or the
    docs — write to <a href="mailto:support@bundu.org">support@bundu.org</a>.
    Security reports go to{" "}
    <a href="mailto:security@nyuchi.com">security@nyuchi.com</a>, as{" "}
    <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a> says, including those
    about the console at <code>app.mzizi.dev</code>. Bugs and proposals are welcome
    as issues on the repository concerned.
  </p>

  <h2>Naming</h2>

  <p>
    The Mzizi wordmark is capitalized: <code>Mzizi</code>. Every other brand
    wordmark in this ecosystem is lowercase: <code>nyuchi</code>,{" "}
    <code>mukoko</code>, <code>shamwari</code>, <code>bundu</code>,{" "}
    <code>nhimbe</code>. Package names, hostnames and code identifiers keep
    their literal spelling. <em>Mzizi</em> is Swahili for root.
  </p>
</Site>
